From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trall9 <tralllll9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:52:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] be7000: rebase onto main 2026-10-22
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ath11k: drop 960 (IPQ9574 support) — upstream 953 is the same Gagniuc
  patch; 962 (no PCIe PME on AHB) stays.
- ath12k: drop 303 (skip unknown direct buffer modules) — upstream 108
  does the same and frees an all-unknown array.
- mac80211 subsys: 393-end-forward-path renumbered to 420 (upstream took 393).
- DTS: upstream ipq9574.dtsi now carries disabled secure-PIL WCSS nodes
  (q6_region, wcss smp2p, q6v5_wcss, wifi0); the BE7000 boots the Q6 with
  the non-secure wcss-pil loader, so delete the upstream nodes. The
  resulting tree matches the running beta4.1 device tree node for node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QwnEsRTxW1M7XMasPGxfRD
